<p><span data-mw-comment-start="" id="c-71.201.123.248-2013-03-03T22:16:00.000Z-Another_call_for_attention_to_this_article."></span>After having been away for some time, I look to see that there has been essentially no substantial progress on this seminal OChem article.
</p><p>How does one argue for all OChem contributors to stop other work, and get the seminal article into shape, then proceed in some orderly fashion with the rest?
</p><p>The article is "not ready for prime time".  It needs serious, focused work.  How cn one spur the attention?  LeProf  <span style="font-size: smaller;" class="autosigned">— Preceding <a href="/wiki/Wikipedia:Signatures" title="Wikipedia:Signatures">unsigned</a> comment added by <a href="/wiki/Special:Contributions/71.201.123.248" title="Special:Contributions/71.201.123.248">71.201.123.248</a> (<a href="/wiki/User_talk:71.201.123.248" title="User talk:71.201.123.248">talk</a>) <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Organic_chemistry#c-71.201.123.248-2013-03-03T22:16:00.000Z-Another_call_for_attention_to_this_article." class="ext-discussiontools-init-timestamplink">22:16, 3 March 2013 (UTC)</a></span><span class="ext-discussiontools-init-replylink-buttons" data-mw-thread-id="c-71.201.123.248-2013-03-03T22:16:00.000Z-Another_call_for_attention_to_this_article."><span class="ext-discussiontools-init-replylink-bracket">[</span><a class="ext-discussiontools-init-replylink-reply" role="button" tabindex="0" href="">reply</a><span class="ext-discussiontools-init-replylink-bracket">]</span><!--__DTELLIPSISBUTTON__{"threadItem":{"timestamp":"2013-03-03T22:16:00.000Z","author":"71.201.123.248","type":"comment","level":1,"id":"c-71.201.123.248-2013-03-03T22:16:00.000Z-Another_call_for_attention_to_this_article.","replies":["c-71.201.123.248-2013-03-03T22:30:00.000Z-71.201.123.248-2013-03-03T22:16:00.000Z"]}}--></span><span data-mw-comment-end="c-71.201.123.248-2013-03-03T22:16:00.000Z-Another_call_for_attention_to_this_article."></span> 
</p>
