<p><span data-mw-comment-start="" id="c-Truthful8-2018-07-09T06:05:00.000Z-Unintelligent_use_of_the_term_organic."></span>Knowing the periodic table of elements is constituted from charged particles, more specifically a proton, electron, and a neutron, how is it possible to explain organic is earthly? A total disregard of an intelligent approach. And the fact that Wikipedia allows this blatant disregard of the truth is irresponsible. Protecting idiocracy? Really? <a href="/wiki/User:Truthful8" title="User:Truthful8">Truthful8</a> (<a href="/wiki/User_talk:Truthful8" title="User talk:Truthful8">talk</a>) <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Organic_chemistry#c-Truthful8-2018-07-09T06:05:00.000Z-Unintelligent_use_of_the_term_organic." class="ext-discussiontools-init-timestamplink">06:05, 9 July 2018 (UTC)</a><span class="ext-discussiontools-init-replylink-buttons" data-mw-thread-id="c-Truthful8-2018-07-09T06:05:00.000Z-Unintelligent_use_of_the_term_organic."><span class="ext-discussiontools-init-replylink-bracket">[</span><a class="ext-discussiontools-init-replylink-reply" role="button" tabindex="0" href="">reply</a><span class="ext-discussiontools-init-replylink-bracket">]</span><!--__DTELLIPSISBUTTON__{"threadItem":{"timestamp":"2018-07-09T06:05:00.000Z","author":"Truthful8","type":"comment","level":1,"id":"c-Truthful8-2018-07-09T06:05:00.000Z-Unintelligent_use_of_the_term_organic.","replies":[]}}--></span><span data-mw-comment-end="c-Truthful8-2018-07-09T06:05:00.000Z-Unintelligent_use_of_the_term_organic."></span>
